agement of dementia with Lewy bodies</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><year>2005</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>1200</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16107351</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muramatsu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nathan</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Recovery of stroke hemiplegia through neurosurgical intervention in the chronic stage</article-title><source>NeuroRehabilitation</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11455092</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakabayashi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Uyama</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoneda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A case of normal pressure hydrocephalus associated with cerebrovascular disorders [Article in Japanese]</article-title><source>No To Shinkei</source><year>1984</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>1077</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6525320</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Relkin</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Marmarou</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Klinge</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Diagnosing idiopathic normalpressure hydrocephalus</article-title><source>Neurosurgery</source><year>2005</year><volume>57</volume><issue>3 Suppl</issue><fpage>S4</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16160425</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Selman</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Spetzler</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Percutaneous lumboperitoneal shunt: review of 130 cases</article-title><source>Neurosurgery</source><year>1980</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7383288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silverberg</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Saul</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Elevated cerebrospinal fluid pressure in patients with Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Cerebrospinal Fluid Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>7</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16737542</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spetzler</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulte</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simplified percutaneous lumboperitoneal shunting</article-title><source>Surg Neurol</source><year>1977</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">831309</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verrees</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Selman</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Management of normal pressure hydrocephalus</article-title><source>Am Fam Physician</source><year>2004</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>1071</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15456116</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walchenbach</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Geiger</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomeer</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The value of temporary external lumbar CSF drainage in predicting the outcome of shunting on normal pressure hydrocephalus</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><year>2002</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>503</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11909911</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wikkelso</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Blomstrand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Normal pressure hydrocephalus. Predictive value of the cerebrospinal fluid tap-test</article-title><source>Acta Neurol Scand</source><year>1986</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>566</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3751498</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yadav</surname><given-names>YR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pande</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Raina</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lumboperitoneal shunts: review of 409 cases</article-title><source>Neurol India</source><year>2004</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>188</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15269466</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>